IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa14-nouns`

-- coa14-ch11-misc.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 17 Chapter 11 "Miscellaneous and supplementary provisions", ss 654 to 657 (lines 8710-8744).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. How to read an answer: see coa14-ch07-premiums.l4 (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE with
-- a FALSE-kind comment, NOTHING with a NOTHING-kind comment).
-- SEAMS: facts another part answers are inputs named for the answering section (s 4(2), s 1121 ...).

§ `Chapter 11 -- Miscellaneous and supplementary provisions`

§§ `s 654 Treatment of reserve arising from reduction of capital`

-- src:8712 | (1) A reserve arising from the reduction of a company's share capital is not distributable, subject to any provision made by order under this section.
@ref s 654(1) Treatment of reserve arising from reduction of capital (src:8712)
GIVEN `the reserve arises from the reduction of the company's share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order under this section provides that the prohibition does not apply to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 654(1) the reserve is distributable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the reserve arises from the reduction of the company's share capital`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "A reserve arising from the reduction of a company's share capital"
        IF `an order under this section provides that the prohibition does not apply to it`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to any provision made by order under this section"; the order (a power of the Secretary of State, subsection (2)) is not among the sources
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A reserve arising from the reduction of a company's share capital is not distributable"

-- s 654(2) and (3): a power of the Secretary of State to make an order (affirmative resolution procedure): machinery, inert (reason 2).

§§ `s 655 Shares no bar to damages against company`

-- src:8718 | A person is not debarred from obtaining damages or other compensation from a company by reason only of his holding or having held shares in the company or any right to apply or subscribe for shares or to be included in the company's register of members ... in respect of shares.
@ref s 655 Shares no bar to damages against company (src:8718)
GIVEN `the only reason is that the person holds or has held shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only reason is that the person holds or has held a right to apply or subscribe for shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only reason is that the person holds or has held a right to be included in the company's register of members in respect of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 655 the person is debarred from obtaining damages or other compensation from the company` MEANS
    IF       `the only reason is that the person holds or has held shares in the company`
         OR `the only reason is that the person holds or has held a right to apply or subscribe for shares`
         OR `the only reason is that the person holds or has held a right to be included in the company's register of members in respect of shares`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not debarred from obtaining damages or other compensation from a company by reason only of his holding or having held shares in the company or any right to apply or subscribe for shares or to be included in the company's register of members ... in respect of shares"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only of": the text says nothing of any other reason for being debarred

§§ `s 656 Public companies: duty of directors to call meeting on serious loss of capital`

-- src:8720 | (1) Where the net assets of a public company are half or less of its called-up share capital, the directors must call a general meeting of the company to consider whether any, and if so what, steps should be taken to deal with the situation.
@ref s 656(1) Public companies: duty of directors to call meeting on serious loss of capital: the duty (src:8720)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the net assets of the company` IS A NUMBER
      `the called-up share capital of the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 656(1) the directors must call a general meeting` MEANS
    IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company` AND `the net assets of the company` TIMES 2 AT MOST `the called-up share capital of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the net assets of a public company are half or less of its called-up share capital, the directors must call a general meeting" ("where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:8721 | (2) They must do so not later than 28 days from the earliest day on which that fact is known to a director of the company.
@ref s 656(2) Public companies: duty of directors to call meeting on serious loss of capital: calling the meeting (src:8721)
GIVEN `the date the fact that the net assets are half or less of the called-up share capital was first known to a director` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 656(2) the last day for the call of the meeting` MEANS `the date the fact that the net assets are half or less of the called-up share capital was first known to a director` PLUS 28

GIVEN `the date the fact that the net assets are half or less of the called-up share capital was first known to a director` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 656(2) the number of days allowed for the call of the meeting` MEANS
    (Day (`s 656(2) the last day for the call of the meeting` `the date the fact that the net assets are half or less of the called-up share capital was first known to a director`)) MINUS (Day `the date the fact that the net assets are half or less of the called-up share capital was first known to a director`)

-- src:8721 | (2) They must do so not later than 28 days from the earliest day on which that fact is known to a director of the company.
@ref s 656(2) Public companies: duty of directors to call meeting on serious loss of capital: calling the meeting: in time (src:8721)
GIVEN `the date the fact that the net assets are half or less of the called-up share capital was first known to a director` IS A DATE
      `the date the directors called the general meeting, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date being asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 656(2) the directors called the general meeting in time` MEANS
    `the answer on the dates`
    WHERE
        `the answer on the dates` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date the directors called the general meeting, if it has`
            WHEN JUST given THEN
                BRANCH
                    IF given LESS THAN `the date the fact that the net assets are half or less of the called-up share capital was first known to a director`
                    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period runs "after" the event and a call of the meeting given before it is not within the period
                    IF given AT MOST `s 656(2) the last day for the call of the meeting` `the date the fact that the net assets are half or less of the called-up share capital was first known to a director`
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "They must do so not later than 28 days from the earliest day on which that fact is known to a director of the company"
            WHEN NOTHING THEN
                IF `the date being asked about` GREATER THAN `s 656(2) the last day for the call of the meeting` `the date the fact that the net assets are half or less of the called-up share capital was first known to a director`
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "They must do so not later than 28 days from the earliest day on which that fact is known to a director of the company" (the period of 28 days has ended and nothing was given)
                ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period of 28 days has not ended, so the text does not yet say whether the duty is met

-- src:8721 | (2) They must do so not later than 28 days from the earliest day on which that fact is known to a director of the company.
@ref s 656(2) Public companies: duty of directors to call meeting on serious loss of capital: calling the meeting: the duty (src:8721)
GIVEN `the number of days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 656(2) the directors' duty to call a general meeting of the company to consider whether any, and if so what, steps should be taken to deal with the situation` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `Action of a party` Director Company "call a general meeting of the company to consider whether any, and if so what, steps should be taken to deal with the situation"
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "the general meeting was not called within 28 days from the earliest day on which the fact was known to a director"


-- src:8722 | (3) The meeting must be convened for a date not later than 56 days from that day.
@ref s 656(3) Public companies: duty of directors to call meeting on serious loss of capital: the date of the meeting (src:8722)
GIVEN `the earliest day on which that fact is known to a director of the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 656(3) the last day for which the meeting may be convened` MEANS `the earliest day on which that fact is known to a director of the company` PLUS 56

-- src:8722 | (3) The meeting must be convened for a date not later than 56 days from that day.
@ref s 656(3) Public companies: duty of directors to call meeting on serious loss of capital: convened for a date in time (src:8722)
GIVEN `the earliest day on which that fact is known to a director of the company` IS A DATE
      `the date for which the meeting is convened` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 656(3) the meeting is convened for a date in time` MEANS
    IF `the date for which the meeting is convened` AT MOST `s 656(3) the last day for which the meeting may be convened` `the earliest day on which that fact is known to a director of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The meeting must be convened for a date not later than 56 days from that day"

-- "failure to convene a meeting as required by this section": the duty arises (subsection (1)) and the calling (subsection (2)) or the date (subsection (3)) fails.
-- src:8723 | (4) If there is a failure to convene a meeting as required by this section, each of the directors of the company who—
@ref s 656(4) Public companies: duty of directors to call meeting on serious loss of capital: a failure to convene (src:8723)
GIVEN `s 656(1) the directors must call a general meeting` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 656(2) the directors called the general meeting in time` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 656(3) the meeting is convened for a date in time` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 656(4) there is a failure to convene a meeting as required by this section` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 656(1) the directors must call a general meeting` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the net assets of a public company are half or less of its called-up share capital, the directors must call a general meeting" (the duty does not arise)
        IF `s 656(1) the directors must call a general meeting` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND (`s 656(2) the directors called the general meeting in time` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 656(3) the meeting is convened for a date in time` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 656(2) the directors called the general meeting in time` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 656(3) the meeting is convened for a date in time` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If there is a failure to convene a meeting as required by this section" (the meeting was called and convened in time)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether there is a failure is not yet known

-- src:8723 | (4) If there is a failure to convene a meeting as required by this section, each of the directors of the company who—
-- src:8724 | (a) knowingly authorises or permits the failure, or
-- src:8725 | (b) after the period during which the meeting should have been convened, knowingly authorises or permits the failure to continue,
-- src:8726 | commits an offence.
@ref s 656(4) Public companies: duty of directors to call meeting on serious loss of capital: the offence (src:8723-8726)
GIVEN `s 656(4) there is a failure to convene a meeting as required by this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the director knowingly authorises or permits the failure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `after the period during which the meeting should have been convened, the director knowingly authorises or permits the failure to continue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 656(4) the director commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 656(4) there is a failure to convene a meeting as required by this section` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If there is a failure to convene a meeting as required by this section, each of the directors ... commits an offence" (there is no such failure)
        IF NOT (`the director knowingly authorises or permits the failure` OR `after the period during which the meeting should have been convened, the director knowingly authorises or permits the failure to continue`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "each of the directors of the company who— (a) knowingly authorises or permits the failure, or (b) after the period during which the meeting should have been convened, knowingly authorises or permits the failure to continue, commits an offence"
        IF `s 656(4) there is a failure to convene a meeting as required by this section` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether there is a failure is not yet known

-- src:8727 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:8728 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:8729 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 656(5) Public companies: duty of directors to call meeting on serious loss of capital: the penalty (src:8727-8729)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Penalty)
`s 656(5) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under this section` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under this section`
    THEN JUST (LIST (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE),
                    (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable"


-- src:8730 | (6) Nothing in this section authorises the consideration at a meeting convened in pursuance of subsection (1) of any matter that could not have been considered at that meeting apart from this section.
@ref s 656(6) Public companies: duty of directors to call meeting on serious loss of capital: the business of the meeting (src:8730)
GIVEN `the matter could not have been considered at that meeting apart from this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 656(6) the section authorises the consideration of the matter at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the matter could not have been considered at that meeting apart from this section`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section authorises the consideration at a meeting convened in pursuance of subsection (1) of any matter that could not have been considered at that meeting apart from this section"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence is about a matter that could not have been considered apart from this section

§§ `s 657 General power to make further provision by regulations`

-- Inert (machinery, reason 2): a regulation-making power of the Secretary of State (affirmative resolution procedure).
